WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:33.490
<b>Miss Buckingham Stussy</b>

3
00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.270
Damn it, I don't understand.

4
00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:51.820
But how are you going to kill...
what you can't understand?

5
00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:57.030
Paper Art.

6
00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:00.070
Afterimage.

7
00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:05.210
My goodness.

8
00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:10.210
You're a wild one, aren't you?

9
00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.210
See, prism stone.

10
00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.450
You backstabbing witch!

11
00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:37.520
I would be a fool to fight
you on even ground.

12
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.490
I know just how strong
you are, after all.

13
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.550
I hope you'll forgive me.

14
00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.870
[chuckles]

15
00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:52.140
[BROOK] What exactly am I
seeing right now?

16
00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:54.960
Why are CP0
fighting each other?

17
00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.680
So, why'd you suddenly
turn on these guys?

18
00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:59.330
[STUSSY chuckles]

19
00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:58.980
You have a falling out?

20
00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:00.820
This is Stussy here.

21
00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.650
[chuckles]
I put both of them to sleep.

22
00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:05.280
What happened to CP0?

23
00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.330
Tell us something, man!

24
00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:11.100
[SHAKA] Seems she even took
Lucci by surprise.

25
00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:14.870
[PYTHAGORAS] Stussy did it.

26
00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:17.130
That's one less thing
to worry about!

27
00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:18.560
[YORK snores]

28
00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:19.560
[YORK] Help me.

29
00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.480
[PYTHAGORAS]
Mother of gastric distention!

30
00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.190
York?

31
00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.280
Say something, York!

32
00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.060
Anything!

33
00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.380
I'm done.

34
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.920
I can't eat another bite.

35
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:30.420
Hey!

36
00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:31.790
Rise and shine, bucko!

37
00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:33.590
We are neck deep
in the soup here!

38
00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:36.050
So, who's this Stussy person?

39
00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.420
[SHAKA] She is a loyal friend,

40
00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:41.180
who's been working undercover
as a CP0 agent for over 20 years.

41
00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:41.960
Undercover?

42
00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:45.020
That's pretty bold, sending
a spy to an intelligence agency!

43
00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:49.450
[SHAKA] It was not part of our original plan,
but that is the way things unfolded.

44
00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.080
[STUSSY] One issue, Doctor.

45
00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.720
I'm afraid my authority
rank is the same as Lucci's.

46
00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.390
I can't override his orders
to the seraphim.

47
00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:06.230
[STUSSY] In other words,
I can't stop them.

48
00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.290
[EDISON] Don't worry, Stussy.

49
00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:11.200
You did great!

50
00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.610
Lilith and I will take
it from here!

51
00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.530
Let's get our giant kids back!

52
00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:17.700
Yes, sir!

53
00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:25.220
[ZORO] We gotta stop those weird
things before it's too late!

54
00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:27.790
At this rate, the whole
crew's gonna get buried!

55
00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:28.820
You're right.

56
00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.490
But this is quite troubling.

57
00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:33.080
They look hauntingly familiar.

58
00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:35.220
[ZORO] Yeah, no kidding.

59
00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:38.430
Especially... him.

60
00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.980
[NAMI yelps]

61
00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:57.430
I'm going to ground them
for a hundred years for this!

62
00:04:57.510 --> 00:04:59.560
[EDISON] Well, at least they made
us a path to the outside!

63
00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:00.390
No mercy!

64
00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.730
[EDISON] No, Lilith, wait!

65
00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:05.140
Just give them an order
like normal, please!

66
00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:08.340
Okay.

67
00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.140
Freedom.

68
00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:13.360
Hey!

69
00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.190
Seraphim!

70
00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.320
Got an order for ya!

71
00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:57.350
Guess you're
different, after all.

72
00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:02.300
He's a cold-blooded killer,
but I almost sense fear from you.

73
00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:07.690
Out with it!

74
00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:08.840
Who are you?

75
00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:15.610
No!

76
00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:19.150
[LILITH whimpers]

77
00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:20.740
That nearly killed me!

78
00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.210
[EDISON] Are you okay, Lilith?

79
00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:24.190
That's it.

80
00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:25.860
I'm putting an end to this!

81
00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:28.100
Seraphim!

82
00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:29.880
This is an order!

83
00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:34.460
[EDISON] Stand down!

84
00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:38.100
Edison!

85
00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:40.490
[LILITH] Edison!

86
00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.890
[chuckles] Right on time!

87
00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.120
[LILITH] You saved me.

88
00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:55.630
[gasps] Edison!

89
00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:59.060
Oh, no.

90
00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.360
Tell me he's okay!

91
00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:12.080
Lilith, darling. Please don't
fret another moment.

92
00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:13.800
Your thing's safe.

93
00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:14.810
[EDISON sighs]

94
00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:17.540
[EDISON grunts]

95
00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:21.030
[EDISON] Holy motility,

96
00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:26.020
Was that a neuropsychiatric
episode or did I see Heaven?

97
00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:43.300
I don't know why, but it seems
like they're done fighting.

98
00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:44.960
Hey!

99
00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:47.430
You wanna tell me
who they hell they are?

100
00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:48.550
Why'd they stop?

101
00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:51.330
Oh, these guys?

102
00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:54.440
They're our sweet little murder
babies and we're so proud of them.

103
00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:56.730
[EDISON] What she means is,
they're our cyborgs.

104
00:07:56.810 --> 00:08:00.940
CP0 gave them an order to attack us,
but our authority is higher,

105
00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:03.570
so when we ordered them to stop,
it overrode the previous command.

106
00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:04.370
Oh.

107
00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:06.410
What's wrong, Mosshead?

108
00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:10.020
Are you havin' trouble keepin'
up with the rest of the class?

109
00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:10.950
[ZORO growls]

110
00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:12.700
[ZORO] Keep up with this,
idiot cook!

111
00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:14.850
[SANJI] Zoro-phim! Deactivate
your dumbass mouth!

112
00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:17.180
Okay, don't talk to me
like I'm a damn cyborg!

113
00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.710
[SANJI, ZORO shouting]

114
00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:17.670
Monster!

115
00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:18.370
Bastard!

116
00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:19.330
Stop!

117
00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:21.680
Well, we survived that mess,
but what's next on the agenda?

118
00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:22.480
[FRANKY] What else?

119
00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:25.400
Dr. Vegapunk gave us
an important mission, remember?

120
00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:27.750
We're gettin' him
off this island safely,

121
00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:30.520
and we're takin' all
his Satellites with us!

122
00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.500
Aww. Heck yeah,
positive vibes!

123
00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:37.250
[FRANKY] Wow! Super!

124
00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:39.190
[STUSSY] Shaka.

125
00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:40.150
[USOPP sighs]

126
00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:44.910
I put Sea Prism Stone
handcuffs on Lucci and Kaku.

127
00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:46.890
[SHAKA]
Excellent work, Stussy.

128
00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:47.790
Thank you.

129
00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:51.160
We're going to have the Straw Hats
take us off the island on their ship.

130
00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:53.510
I think it would be wise
for you to come with us.

131
00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:54.310
– [STUSSY] Agreed.
– [NAMI] Ugh.

132
00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.030
[USOPP] Stop inviting people
into our house!

133
00:08:57.110 --> 00:08:57.780
Who raised you?

134
00:08:57.780 --> 00:08:58.620
Cut it.

135
00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:02.510
[LUFFY] Hey!

136
00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:04.270
Bonney!

137
00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:07.230
Mr. Appleman!

138
00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:08.200
Where'd you go?

139
00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:09.990
[CHOPPER] Luffy!

140
00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:11.800
[LUFFY] Hey, Chopper!

141
00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:13.240
You find 'em?

142
00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.810
No, it's like they disappeared.

143
00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:16.740
[LUFFY] This is weird.

144
00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.910
I hope nothing bad happened.

145
00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:20.300
[CHOPPER] I'll check this way.

146
00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:21.020
Good luck!

147
00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:22.040
[LUFFY] You too!

148
00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:22.950
[CHOPPER] Thanks!

149
00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:24.930
[LUFFY] Man, what a mess.

150
00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:27.520
Stop hiding already!

151
00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:26.930
Hey!

152
00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:30.280
We can't set sail without you!

153
00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:33.400
[NARRATOR] The Straw Hats
encountered Bonney

154
00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.800
at sea and rescued
her from a floating eddy.

155
00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:39.190
Afterwards they all traveled
to the Future Island, Egghead.

156
00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:42.290
But their plan encountered
an unexpected snag.

157
00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:44.040
Old man!

158
00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:52.760
[NARRATOR] Dr.
Vegapunk Stella... disappeared.

159
00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:58.400
[NARRATOR] This is Sphinx,
in the New World.

160
00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:01.870
It's the hometown of the famous
pirate Whitebeard.

161
00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.850
I was so scared!

162
00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:10.230
I'm so glad you're
back, Marco!

163
00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.900
I wasn't scared at all,
for the record!

164
00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:15.970
[BOY A] The Navy came barging
in here outta nowhere!

165
00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.480
[MARCO] I'm sorry, you guys.

166
00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:19.620
That does sound scary.

167
00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:22.180
I wish I'd been here to protect
you from those jerks!

168
00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:24.070
[BOY B] Okay, but I said
I wasn't scared.

169
00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:26.280
So, tell me, what did they do?

170
00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:27.650
[BOY A] All sorts of stuff!

171
00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.560
Those Marines were horrible!

172
00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:30.290
Huh?

173
00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:32.020
They wanted
Whitebeard's treasure!

174
00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.560
They were gonna steal it!

175
00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:35.740
<b>Several Days Ago</b>

176
00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:35.350
Just like a buncha pirates!

177
00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:39.270
[BOTH gasp]

178
00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:40.030
Huh?

179
00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:43.960
Huh?

180
00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:59.740
[TOWNSPEOPLE scream]

181
00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:04.570
Drag out the villagers
and gather them all here.

182
00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:05.450
[MARINES] Yes, sir!

183
00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:14.610
[RATEL] I won't harm you as long
as you do what I say.

184
00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:18.080
Which is quite generous of me,
since you're not protected by the law,

185
00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:21.480
and this island's independent from
the World Government, right?

186
00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:25.560
I believe Whitebeard's treasure is
hidden somewhere in this country.

187
00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:27.510
Tell me where it is, now!

188
00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:28.290
[CITIZEN C] Stop this!

189
00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:29.920
We don't know what
you're talking about!

190
00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:32.840
This is the first time I've
heard of any treasure!

191
00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:33.930
[RATEL] Oh, well...

192
00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:37.300
That's that, I suppose.

193
00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:42.500
I swear...

194
00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:44.680
[RATEL] You know what I
call your defiance?

195
00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:48.360
An act of aggression against
the World Government!

196
00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:51.300
So let's do it this way.

197
00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:55.960
I'm going to shoot
you one by one.

198
00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:58.240
Till you lead me
to the treasure!

199
00:11:58.600 --> 00:11:59.730
[BOY B wails]

200
00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:00.320
Stop it!

201
00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:01.990
The treasure doesn't exist!

202
00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:04.790
Please don't point
a gun at my brother!

203
00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:09.200
We may not be able to afford your taxes,
but we're still are human beings!

204
00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:11.390
Don't treat us like animals!

205
00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:12.640
[RATEL] You're not scared?

206
00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:16.140
I know Marco isn't here
to protect you right now.

207
00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:18.620
[RATEL] Restrain her!

208
00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:20.450
[CITIZEN B]
What are you doing?

209
00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:21.810
Let me go!

210
00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:23.500
[BOY B] Grandma, no!

211
00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:24.510
You brutes!

212
00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:25.920
Get your hands off me!

213
00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:28.560
Leave her alone!

214
00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:30.270
She's not a threat!

215
00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.600
Don't you hurt her!

216
00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:34.840
Stop it!

217
00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:36.350
Let them go!

218
00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:39.510
[chuckles] Huh?

219
00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:43.970
Ahhhhhhh! [yelling]

220
00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:52.790
[RATEL yells]

221
00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:05.670
Don't mess with
my daddy's hometown!

222
00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:07.660
Or I'll smash you!

223
00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:11.040
[MARINE A]
It's Edward Weevil!

224
00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:15.060
[MARINE C] Yeah, let's go!

225
00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:16.320
Just leave her!

226
00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:18.110
[MARINE D] Why is he here?

227
00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:21.700
I thought we sent troops to arrest him
when they shut down the Seven Warlords!

228
00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:24.250
[MARINE E] Yeah, but those troops were
never heard from again!

229
00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:24.920
[MARINE F] No way.

230
00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:26.070
He beat them all?

231
00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:27.260
That's no man!

232
00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:28.720
He's a monster!

233
00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:30.320
Retreat to the ship for now!

234
00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:32.090
We'll wait for reinforcements!

235
00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:33.370
[MARINE H] This is Sphinx!

236
00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:36.490
We were attacked by the former
Warlord, Edward Weevil!

237
00:13:36.570 --> 00:13:37.810
We need backup!

238
00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:38.860
Hurry!

239
00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:42.330
And then
the Marines went away.

240
00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:44.060
They just waited out at sea.

241
00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:47.910
We're lucky that big guy
showed up when he did

242
00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.210
'cause they were
really gonna shoot us, right?

243
00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:53.110
So he saved the day, huh?

244
00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.160
I'm really glad everyone
made it out safe!

245
00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:57.290
That's not the end
of the story, Marco!

246
00:13:57.370 --> 00:14:00.240
Someone else showed up
and ruined everything!

247
00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:02.950
Navy Admiral Ryokugyu!

248
00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:09.360
My precious Weevil resisted so bravely,
but that rat took him away!

249
00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:10.650
[BUCKIN] Weevil!

250
00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:11.950
[WEEVIL] Mommy!

251
00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.370
[BUCKIN] You're going to help
me get my son back!

252
00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:18.350
My son.

253
00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:24.050
<b>Miss Buckin
Freeloader at MADS
Self-Proclaimed Scientist
Ex-Rocks Pirates Member</b>

254
00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:20.820
And my treasure!

255
00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:23.000
Edward Newgate's
inheritance will be mine!

256
00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:23.760
You hear me?

257
00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:27.850
<b>Real Name:
Buckingham Stussy</b>

258
00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:25.090
Mine!

259
00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:35.210
No, I'm just worried sick about my sweet
boy, who sacrificed his freedom

260
00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:36.490
for his daddy's village!

261
00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:39.760
Oh, Newgate, what have
they done to our baby?

262
00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:39.100
[sighs]

263
00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.420
At any rate,
I guess I owe him one.

264
00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:46.830
I'm glad he was
here for the village.

265
00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.250
I know that tone!

266
00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:51.920
You're just like all the others.

267
00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:55.780
You don't believe Weevil is
Whitebeard's real son, do you?

268
00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:58.100
Well, I know someone
who can prove it!

269
00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:01.640
Huh? Dr. Vegapunk
will show you all!

270
00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:12.470
Admiral!

271
00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:15.290
We brought teacakes
for your meeting, as you requested!

272
00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:18.440
[KIZARU] Ah, you've tested them
for poison, I assume?

273
00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:19.230
[MARINE I] Of course!

274
00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:21.010
[KIZARU]
I'll take it from here.

275
00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:22.120
At ease, kid.

276
00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:23.000
Sir!

277
00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:34.400
[knocking]

278
00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:37.700
Pardon the intrusion.

279
00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:41.850
I thought you could use
some refreshments.

280
00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:44.160
Allow me to serve you.

281
00:15:51.270 --> 00:15:53.030
[KIZARU]
I've been meaning to ask you.

282
00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:56.240
Have you ever met Dr.
Vegapunk before?

283
00:15:57.410 --> 00:15:58.330
[SATURN] I have.

284
00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:05.010
[SATURN] Just once.

285
00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:07.270
A long time ago.

286
00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:10.110
It's hard to believe
that he betrayed you.

287
00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:12.670
Not a bright move
for a genius.

288
00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:23.380
<b>St. Jaygarcia Saturn
The Five Elders, Supreme Council of the World Government</b>

289
00:16:23.470 --> 00:16:25.380
Yes, I must say,

290
00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:24.890
[AGENTS scream]

291
00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.560
This is quite the regrettable
turn of events.

292
00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:32.970
It can't be!

293
00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.850
<b>Fabriophase
Egghead</b>

294
00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:44.650
A pacifista?

295
00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:46.020
What's wrong with it?

296
00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:46.560
Hey!

297
00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:47.260
Stop it!

298
00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:49.180
You're attacking
the wrong guys!

299
00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:51.080
We're with
the Government, too!

300
00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:52.290
Hey!

301
00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:53.540
Did you hear what I said?

302
00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:54.660
Shut up!

303
00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:07.770
Die, you monster!

304
00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:11.030
[AGENT O] Wait!

305
00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:13.240
Don't shoot!

306
00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:14.120
No!

307
00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:18.290
Ahhhh!

308
00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:20.690
[gasps]

309
00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.130
What the hell did he just do?

310
00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:34.240
It looked like
a Bubble Shield!

311
00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:36.850
They say that's one of Vegapunk's
greatest inventions.

312
00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:38.740
It has the power
to repel anything!

313
00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:39.400
Damn it.

314
00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:41.320
It's nothing like
the ones in Marineford.

315
00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:42.640
It's a brand new model.

316
00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:44.780
The pacifista Mark III!

317
00:17:56.850 --> 00:17:59.810
<b>y432lumoctvBNOG
S29wu,8jF0RQDUb 0UKVbdqBJCgONNL
sLcWKaSjD;F8r!l</b>
<b>Combat Weapon of Marines' Science Group</b>

318
00:17:57.140 --> 00:17:59.580
Submit and relocate to Factory B.

319
00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:05.410
[PACIFISTA]
Hostile activity confirmed.

320
00:18:08.780 --> 00:18:10.280
We're all gonna die.

321
00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:11.880
Please, don't shoot!

322
00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:13.160
We surrender!

323
00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:21.450
You are under arrest.

324
00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:27.120
Please, just wait!

325
00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:29.720
Pacifistas never make
decisions on their own!

326
00:18:30.070 --> 00:18:31.860
Who's giving you
these orders?

327
00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:36.260
<b>Fabrio</b>

328
00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:39.240
[CITIZEN B]
Please don't move.

329
00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:40.730
You'll open your wounds.

330
00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:46.270
[CITIZENS chattering]

331
00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:45.490
And this was supposed
to be my day off.

332
00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:47.100
How is the pacifista?

333
00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:48.570
Is it doing its job?

334
00:18:51.490 --> 00:18:53.810
Something bad is
happening up there.

335
00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:55.210
Punk, do you copy?

336
00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:56.150
It's me!

337
00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:59.200
[static]

338
00:18:58.220 --> 00:18:58.880
Punk?

339
00:18:58.880 --> 00:18:59.960
Say something!

340
00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:03.400
He can't hear me.

341
00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:04.750
The Dome is closed.

342
00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:05.730
We're shut out.

343
00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:07.500
I'm sorry, Punk.

344
00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.000
I can't protect you.

345
00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:10.110
Go!

346
00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:11.440
And take care of Punk!

347
00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:12.350
You hear me?

348
00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:14.650
Okay!

349
00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:15.610
Leave it to me!

350
00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:21.390
[SENTOMARU] The Navy hasn't
stopped communication,

351
00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:23.420
but they've cut us
out of the loop.

352
00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:24.870
Guess that tells us
where we stand.

353
00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:25.830
[CITIZENS gasp]

354
00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:25.700
Yeah.

355
00:19:29.090 --> 00:19:32.580
In the world's eyes,
I'm already a traitor.

356
00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:38.490
Might as well do
as I please, then.

357
00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:42.630
Pacifista Mark III, activate!

358
00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:47.020
[alarm blares]

359
00:19:52.740 --> 00:19:55.370
[SENTOMARU]
All 50 units, dispatch!

360
00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:57.430
Oh...

361
00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:01.420
[SENTOMARU] Straw Hat Luffy is
going to take Dr

362
00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:03.800
Vegapunk off the island
aboard his ship!

363
00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:07.230
Your mission is to make
sure it departs safely!

364
00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:08.360
[PACIFISTAS] Understood.

365
00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:14.840
[SENTOMARU]
The Navy is up to something!

366
00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:17.440
Keep an eye on the shore!

367
00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.490
Something big is
about to happen.

368
00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:23.370
Dr. Vegapunk is
your creator. Protect him.

369
00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:24.600
Protect him.

370
00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:27.710
No matter what,
get him off this island!

371
00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:33.380
<b>The P.A.W. Room
Inside the Lab</b>

372
00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:32.010
[VEGAPUNK] Bonney, please.

373
00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:33.520
I'm begging you.

374
00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:35.370
[BONNEY] I've heard
enough out of you!

375
00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:37.690
– [thud]
– [VEGAPUNK screams]

376
00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:37.950
Bonney!

377
00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:36.250
Are you all right?

378
00:21:36.630 --> 00:21:42.070
Hey. What happened to you?

379
00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:42.710
[BOY] It's over.

380
00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:46.330
I tried, but I just can't!

381
00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:48.520
[gasps]

382
00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:50.510
Is that you, Dad?

383
00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:53.120
Look!

384
00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:55.600
Look!

385
00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:03.030
Thought you could run, boy?

386
00:22:03.110 --> 00:22:04.870
Get on your damn feet!

387
00:22:04.950 --> 00:22:05.760
Now!

388
00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:06.870
No, please!

389
00:22:06.950 --> 00:22:07.780
Go away!

390
00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:09.580
Stop your whining!

391
00:22:09.660 --> 00:22:10.990
You're coming with us!

392
00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:13.660
[yells]

393
00:22:13.660 --> 00:22:15.920
[screams]

394
00:22:15.210 --> 00:22:17.050
[KUMA] No! I'm begging you!

395
00:22:17.630 --> 00:22:19.650
Let me go!

396
00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:21.730
Someone help me! Please!

397
00:22:21.810 --> 00:22:22.610
Help me!

398
00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:23.850
Stop squirming!

399
00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:25.000
Move it!

400
00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:25.810
Come on!

401
00:22:25.890 --> 00:22:27.460
We're not letting you go!

402
00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:29.960
If you escape, they're
gonna execute us all!

403
00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:31.540
But I... I can't!

404
00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:32.720
I don't wanna go back.

405
00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:34.320
I don't wanna go back there!

406
00:22:34.400 --> 00:22:35.220
Help me!

407
00:22:36.470 --> 00:22:38.710
Please go away!

408
00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:40.170
Somebody help! Shut your damn mouth!

409
00:22:44.410 --> 00:22:44.990
[growls] Let him go!

410
00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:47.190
Just leave me!

411
00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.180
Please don't make
me go back!

412
00:22:51.060 --> 00:22:52.230
Stop it!

413
00:22:52.310 --> 00:22:53.970
He said he doesn't want to!

414
00:22:56.250 --> 00:22:58.040
[KUMA yells]

415
00:22:58.040 --> 00:22:58.840
[BONNEY] Wait!

416
00:22:59.470 --> 00:23:00.590
What's happening?

417
00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:03.030
Why can't I get closer?

418
00:23:07.600 --> 00:23:10.260
Stop your crying,
you little shit!

419
00:23:14.070 --> 00:23:15.330
[KUMA]
I can't take it anymore.

420
00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:16.810
I'd rather die!

421
00:23:17.420 --> 00:23:18.320
You're too strong!

422
00:23:18.340 --> 00:23:18.910
[VIGILANTE D] Come here!

423
00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:19.750
[KUMA] No!

424
00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:21.730
– [VIGILANTE C] Bastard!
– [KUMA] I'll never go back!

425
00:23:22.230 --> 00:23:24.070
You might as well just kill me!

426
00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:27.730
If I go back, I'll end
up dead anyway!

427
00:23:29.690 --> 00:23:30.450
[BONNEY] What?

428
00:23:30.530 --> 00:23:31.870
Shut up, kid!

429
00:23:31.870 --> 00:23:33.540
[yells]

430
00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:36.150
Stop it!

431
00:23:37.250 --> 00:23:38.050
Nooooooo!

432
00:23:38.710 --> 00:23:40.960
[KUMA yells]

433
00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:41.650
Nooooooo!

434
00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:47.170
[VIGILANTES grunting]

435
00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:53.610
[VIGILANTE E] Come on!

436
00:23:53.690 --> 00:23:54.650
Stop it!

437
00:23:55.390 --> 00:23:56.390
You monsters!

438
00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:04.910
[KUMA] It hurts.

439
00:24:06.270 --> 00:24:09.430
I'm sorry!
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

440
00:24:12.070 --> 00:24:13.310
That's enough!

441
00:24:13.670 --> 00:24:14.530
Let him go!

442
00:24:28.230 --> 00:24:30.850
[BONNEY]
No. I can't watch this anymore.

443
00:24:31.470 --> 00:24:35.110
I can't take it!

444
00:24:32.260 --> 00:24:33.970
[BOTH yell]

445
00:24:35.190 --> 00:24:36.730
Someone help me!

446
00:24:37.630 --> 00:24:38.430
[BONNEY] No more.

447
00:24:40.430 --> 00:24:41.370
Please, no more.

448
00:24:41.830 --> 00:24:43.630
Stop hurting him!

449
00:25:02.450 --> 00:25:04.070
Shoot him down!

450
00:25:14.640 --> 00:25:16.440
[MARINE A] Is continuing
to climb the Red Line!

451
00:25:16.510 --> 00:25:18.920
He appears to be
heading for Mary Geoise!

452
00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:21.840
Do not let him enter the Holy
Land, no matter the cost!

453
00:25:21.920 --> 00:25:24.390
The Navy's reputation
is at stake!

454
00:25:24.470 --> 00:25:26.520
This is our sworn duty!

455
00:25:33.880 --> 00:25:35.510
[BONNEY] My father's past.

456
00:25:36.570 --> 00:25:38.400
I don't know if I can face it.

457
00:25:40.280 --> 00:25:42.570
I don't know if I
have the strength.

458
00:25:46.750 --> 00:25:47.770
[BONNEY] But I have to.

459
00:25:49.430 --> 00:25:52.560
I need to I need
to find out the truth!

460
00:25:55.090 --> 00:25:55.890
Okay.

461
00:25:56.380 --> 00:25:57.260
I'm ready, Dad.

462
00:26:01.520 --> 00:26:02.730
Show me again.

463
00:26:03.400 --> 00:26:04.200
I'll stay.

464
00:26:11.220 --> 00:26:15.640
<b>Labophase
Egghead</b>

465
00:26:11.490 --> 00:26:13.470
[USOPP] What do you mean you
couldn't find Vegapunk?

466
00:26:13.470 --> 00:26:15.670
There are only so many
places he can be!

467
00:26:15.750 --> 00:26:18.240
Maybe there's some secret
passageway you didn't see?

468
00:26:18.240 --> 00:26:19.110
There must be!

469
00:26:22.360 --> 00:26:23.220
No.

470
00:26:23.300 --> 00:26:24.600
He's gone.

471
00:26:25.060 --> 00:26:27.760
I ran everywhere
lookin' for the guy...

472
00:26:29.280 --> 00:26:32.470
And now I'm dyin'
and he's still lost.

473
00:26:32.550 --> 00:26:33.330
Oh, come on.

474
00:26:33.410 --> 00:26:34.090
Really?

475
00:26:34.090 --> 00:26:35.020
Yes, really!

476
00:26:35.100 --> 00:26:37.330
The hover function
on his shoes stopped working!

477
00:26:37.330 --> 00:26:38.430
I think he broke them.

478
00:26:38.510 --> 00:26:39.770
Hey, don't tell people that!

479
00:26:39.770 --> 00:26:41.700
They're gonna make
me pay for new ones!

480
00:26:41.700 --> 00:26:43.390
Nobody cares about
the damn shoes!

481
00:26:43.390 --> 00:26:44.560
We're all about to die!

482
00:26:44.640 --> 00:26:46.900
If he's not in the lab, then
where could he have gone?

483
00:26:46.900 --> 00:26:48.660
[SANJI]
Just chill out a sec, Usopp.

484
00:26:48.740 --> 00:26:50.110
[USOPP] We don't have a sec!

485
00:26:50.190 --> 00:26:53.820
If we don't leave now, they're gonna send
a whole fleet of those suit-wearing sadists

486
00:26:53.820 --> 00:26:54.470
after us!

487
00:26:54.470 --> 00:26:57.060
We know, but we can't
leave without Vegapunk.

488
00:26:56.960 --> 00:26:58.180
[LUFFY groans]

489
00:26:58.160 --> 00:27:00.850
What the heck are you tryin'
to pull, Mister Apple Man?

490
00:27:00.850 --> 00:27:02.300
Bonney's missing, too.

491
00:27:02.380 --> 00:27:04.200
Maybe she's calmed
down by now.

492
00:27:04.630 --> 00:27:05.810
[SHAKA] I know where she is.

493
00:27:07.580 --> 00:27:09.640
[SHAKA] I can see her right
here on the monitor.

494
00:27:09.720 --> 00:27:10.900
Wait, you found her?

495
00:27:10.980 --> 00:27:11.780
[SHAKA] Never lost her.

496
00:27:11.860 --> 00:27:12.920
[STRAW HATS] Never lost her?

497
00:27:15.110 --> 00:27:15.810
[ZORO] Hey.

498
00:27:15.870 --> 00:27:16.990
What a mess.

499
00:27:17.990 --> 00:27:18.920
Hm? Zoro!

500
00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:20.680
I thought we were settin' sail.

501
00:27:20.760 --> 00:27:22.870
What are you doin' just
sittin' around in here?

502
00:27:22.870 --> 00:27:24.680
Well, we kinda
had some issues.

503
00:27:24.760 --> 00:27:27.590
Well, I wouldn't blame you
for wanting to dilly-dally a bit!

504
00:27:27.590 --> 00:27:28.400
Just look!

505
00:27:28.480 --> 00:27:30.110
It's all so futuristic!

506
00:27:30.190 --> 00:27:30.810
[CHOPPER] Wow!

507
00:27:30.810 --> 00:27:31.610
I'll say!

508
00:27:32.070 --> 00:27:35.070
They even invented a high-tech
hat that shows off your afro!

509
00:27:35.120 --> 00:27:37.080
A fishbowl is your idea
of high-tech?

510
00:27:37.160 --> 00:27:37.960
Really?

511
00:27:38.350 --> 00:27:39.790
This is quite a wreck.

512
00:27:41.700 --> 00:27:43.810
Shaka, how's Atlas doing?

513
00:27:43.890 --> 00:27:44.750
[SHAKA] Let me see.

514
00:27:44.830 --> 00:27:46.670
Edison, Lilith. Status report.

515
00:27:46.750 --> 00:27:47.730
The status is?!

516
00:27:47.810 --> 00:27:48.960
You still suck!

517
00:27:49.360 --> 00:27:50.060
[EDISON] Move, Lilith.

518
00:27:50.100 --> 00:27:52.300
I just finished the repairs
on Atlas, Shaka!

519
00:27:52.350 --> 00:27:53.080
Come see!

520
00:27:53.160 --> 00:27:53.660
We!

521
00:27:53.660 --> 00:27:55.810
Plural! We just
finished the repairs!

522
00:27:55.890 --> 00:27:57.700
I worked on her just
as much as you did!

523
00:27:57.700 --> 00:27:58.470
Yes, sir!

524
00:27:58.550 --> 00:28:00.860
Hey, gang!

525
00:28:01.350 --> 00:28:02.360
Guess who's back?

526
00:28:02.440 --> 00:28:05.560
I'm fixed up and ready to go!

527
00:28:06.760 --> 00:28:08.130
[yells]

528
00:28:07.660 --> 00:28:08.490
Damn Atlas!

529
00:28:08.920 --> 00:28:09.750
Oh, no!

530
00:28:11.380 --> 00:28:12.280
Lilith, look!

531
00:28:12.360 --> 00:28:13.190
I'm alive!

532
00:28:13.930 --> 00:28:15.120
[LILITH] Yes, I can see that!

533
00:28:15.200 --> 00:28:17.140
[EDISON]
Gosh, she sure is full of energy!

534
00:28:17.220 --> 00:28:18.700
I guess we did a good job!

535
00:28:25.080 --> 00:28:25.770
Hey, girl.

536
00:28:25.770 --> 00:28:27.410
Hey. Lookin' good.

537
00:28:27.490 --> 00:28:27.980
Thanks.

538
00:28:27.980 --> 00:28:29.230
Did you just wake up now?

539
00:28:29.240 --> 00:28:30.600
You kind of missed a lot!

540
00:28:30.680 --> 00:28:33.350
If you want, I'll smack
the drowsies right out of you!

541
00:28:33.350 --> 00:28:36.410
How 'bout you don't
and say you did?

542
00:28:34.080 --> 00:28:35.080
[chuckles]

543
00:28:39.150 --> 00:28:40.040
Oh, good.

544
00:28:40.120 --> 00:28:41.740
I'm glad her face got better.

545
00:28:41.540 --> 00:28:43.750
[SANJI yells]

546
00:28:41.820 --> 00:28:43.600
[EDISON] We had replacement
parts ready.

547
00:28:43.680 --> 00:28:44.510
Oh! Hey!

548
00:28:45.200 --> 00:28:46.160
It's you!

549
00:28:46.240 --> 00:28:48.440
You're the little guy
who saved my bacon!

550
00:28:48.520 --> 00:28:49.520
Thanks a bunch, bud!

551
00:28:49.580 --> 00:28:50.310
No prob!

552
00:28:51.770 --> 00:28:54.390
So you've started beating
up little girls now, huh?

553
00:28:54.470 --> 00:28:58.050
You creeps are every bit as rotten
as you were when we first met you!

554
00:28:58.130 --> 00:29:02.540
If you so much as look at Robin again,
I'll put you straight in the ground!

555
00:29:02.880 --> 00:29:03.500
[ROBIN] Nami.

556
00:29:03.500 --> 00:29:04.200
Huh?

557
00:29:04.240 --> 00:29:06.510
There's nothing they
can do to me now.

558
00:29:06.590 --> 00:29:10.530
That said, I wanted to see Stella,
but it seems something happened?

559
00:29:10.900 --> 00:29:14.770
[SHAKA] Unfortunately, we've been faced
with two unpleasant surprises.

560
00:29:14.850 --> 00:29:17.540
First: Stella has disappeared.

561
00:29:18.120 --> 00:29:20.940
And Second: We've lost control
of the Frontier Dome.

562
00:29:21.980 --> 00:29:22.970
Huh?

563
00:29:23.050 --> 00:29:24.870
And what does
that mean for us?

564
00:29:25.690 --> 00:29:30.460
[SHAKA] It means, for the time being, we're
trapped inside the Labophase with no escape.

565
00:29:30.340 --> 00:29:31.880
[BOTH gasp]

566
00:29:31.880 --> 00:29:35.700
[SHAKA] If anyone tries to leave, laser beams
will incinerate them immediately.

567
00:29:35.780 --> 00:29:37.040
Are you kidding me?!

568
00:29:37.120 --> 00:29:40.460
We're supposed to take Vegapunk
to sea like, urgently, aren't we?

569
00:29:40.540 --> 00:29:43.080
[SHAKA] Ideally, but we can't do
that while he's missing.

570
00:29:43.160 --> 00:29:45.080
[USOPP] Then what are we
supposed to do?!

571
00:29:45.920 --> 00:29:47.340
[SHAKA]
Let me handle the Dome.

572
00:29:47.420 --> 00:29:48.770
You go look for Stella.

573
00:29:49.450 --> 00:29:51.940
That's the only solution
afforded to us.

574
00:29:52.020 --> 00:29:53.070
Quick question.

575
00:29:53.150 --> 00:29:56.940
You got monitors that show the whole lab,
but you said you can't see Vegapunk on 'em,

576
00:29:56.940 --> 00:29:59.290
so what's the point in us
searchin' the place?

577
00:29:59.370 --> 00:30:02.610
[SHAKA] Normally, we can see everything,
but not at the moment.

578
00:30:03.030 --> 00:30:06.090
The seraphim's rampage did
quite a number on this place.

579
00:30:06.170 --> 00:30:09.410
Many of the Cam-snails are
either lost or unconscious.

580
00:30:10.440 --> 00:30:13.320
We need everyone to check
the unsurveilled areas.

581
00:30:13.760 --> 00:30:17.700
Stella could be incapacitated
in one of the Cam-snail blind spots.

582
00:30:18.280 --> 00:30:20.240
[PYTHAGORAS]
Shaka. This is Pythagoras.

583
00:30:20.320 --> 00:30:23.820
I'm on the third floor of Building C,
and it's crickets up here.

584
00:30:23.900 --> 00:30:24.700
[SHAKA] I see.

585
00:30:25.060 --> 00:30:27.580
Then check the next building
over, while you're there.

586
00:30:27.580 --> 00:30:29.030
[NAMI]
We should start looking, too.

587
00:30:29.110 --> 00:30:31.910
The sooner we get out of here
the better, after all.

588
00:30:31.990 --> 00:30:34.940
And I might find some future
treasure along the way!

589
00:30:35.020 --> 00:30:36.410
That sounds delightful!

590
00:30:36.490 --> 00:30:37.640
I think I'll come, too!

591
00:30:37.680 --> 00:30:39.490
[EDISON] Hey, I don't like
the sound of that!

592
00:30:39.570 --> 00:30:41.520
You guys aren't gonna
start any trouble, are you?

593
00:30:41.520 --> 00:30:43.580
[BROOK]
We would never! Right, Nami?

594
00:30:43.990 --> 00:30:45.240
[NAMI]
Yeah, let's go with that.

595
00:30:45.240 --> 00:30:46.610
[EDISON]
That wasn't convincing at all.

596
00:30:46.610 --> 00:30:47.860
Stay where I can see you!

597
00:30:48.070 --> 00:30:49.800
If you don't mind,
I'll search as well.

598
00:30:49.800 --> 00:30:51.890
It's not like him
to disappear like this.

599
00:30:51.970 --> 00:30:53.610
Mind if I come
along with you?

600
00:30:53.690 --> 00:30:54.480
Of course.

601
00:30:54.560 --> 00:30:55.280
I'm grateful.

602
00:30:55.360 --> 00:30:56.100
Susie!

603
00:30:57.130 --> 00:30:58.610
Let me come, too, please!

604
00:30:58.690 --> 00:31:01.150
I'll follow you
to the ends of the earth!

605
00:31:01.230 --> 00:31:02.030
[ZORO] Alright.

606
00:31:02.540 --> 00:31:04.050
Guess I'd better go, too.

607
00:31:04.390 --> 00:31:05.480
Hold up, Mosshead!

608
00:31:05.560 --> 00:31:06.500
What's your deal?

609
00:31:06.580 --> 00:31:08.480
I'm lookin' for some
apple guy, right?

610
00:31:08.550 --> 00:31:09.400
Easy.

611
00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:10.500
Not for you!

612
00:31:10.580 --> 00:31:11.480
No way!

613
00:31:11.940 --> 00:31:13.140
Absolutely not!

614
00:31:13.220 --> 00:31:14.170
Well, knock it off!

615
00:31:14.200 --> 00:31:15.660
What the hell is your problem?

616
00:31:15.660 --> 00:31:18.800
If you're out searching, then
who's gonna search for you?

617
00:31:18.880 --> 00:31:19.960
[ZORO] Come on, man.

618
00:31:20.320 --> 00:31:21.000
Sanji's right!

619
00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:22.670
Zoro, please don't go.

620
00:31:22.750 --> 00:31:23.520
[ZORO] You too?

621
00:31:23.600 --> 00:31:24.320
No, really.

622
00:31:24.400 --> 00:31:26.000
Be a good boy and stay here.

623
00:31:26.410 --> 00:31:27.210
[ZORO] Whatever.

624
00:31:27.560 --> 00:31:29.620
Let's get our search
on, my bros!

625
00:31:29.700 --> 00:31:31.410
I won't let Vegapunk down!

626
00:31:31.490 --> 00:31:33.040
But it's like a maze out there!

627
00:31:33.080 --> 00:31:35.130
I've got a really bad
feeling about this!

628
00:31:35.200 --> 00:31:37.770
Even if we're not Zoro,
we still might get lost!

629
00:31:37.850 --> 00:31:40.370
[LILITH] How did you guys ever
make it out of a port?

630
00:31:40.450 --> 00:31:41.550
Just follow me!

631
00:31:41.630 --> 00:31:42.330
[USOPP] Really?

632
00:31:42.390 --> 00:31:43.190
Thanks!

633
00:31:44.160 --> 00:31:45.620
York, are you asleep again?

634
00:31:45.700 --> 00:31:46.400
We need help.

635
00:31:46.480 --> 00:31:48.480
You can nap once
we're on the ship. Get!

636
00:31:50.690 --> 00:31:53.190
[yawns]

637
00:31:57.610 --> 00:32:02.080
[ZORO] Don't know why they wanted me to stick around
so bad, but I guess it's fine.

638
00:32:03.020 --> 00:32:06.030
I'm sure findin' one old man
won't be too hard for them.

639
00:32:06.110 --> 00:32:08.400
But damn, you really
went all out, huh?

640
00:32:10.120 --> 00:32:11.180
[groans] I always...

641
00:32:12.270 --> 00:32:13.850
...go all out.

642
00:32:13.930 --> 00:32:15.210
Yeah, fair enough.

643
00:32:15.890 --> 00:32:19.010
Anyway, I never thought I'd
see these assholes again.

644
00:32:19.360 --> 00:32:20.760
Really takes me back.

645
00:32:20.840 --> 00:32:22.290
Remember Water Seven?

646
00:32:22.370 --> 00:32:23.700
Ice Pops' place!

647
00:32:23.780 --> 00:32:25.310
I wonder how he's doin'.

648
00:32:32.480 --> 00:32:35.410
[MORGANS] Now there's a scoop
if I ever heard one!

649
00:32:35.490 --> 00:32:38.350
Who would've thunk
the Government's power-drunk,

650
00:32:38.350 --> 00:32:40.310
and they're coming
for Vegapunk!

651
00:32:40.820 --> 00:32:43.440
Gunning for the greatest
minds in the world again?

652
00:32:43.520 --> 00:32:46.510
Seems Ohara was a big
enough hit to get a sequel.

653
00:32:46.590 --> 00:32:48.890
But they'll be
hard-pressed to spin this.

654
00:32:48.970 --> 00:32:51.760
Vegapunk's a hero
all across the seas!

655
00:32:51.840 --> 00:32:53.690
He brought light
to towns all around!

656
00:32:53.710 --> 00:32:56.460
His energy tech made
him a shining star!

657
00:32:56.540 --> 00:32:58.910
But he's sharing
the stage on Egghead...

658
00:32:58.990 --> 00:33:00.130
...with him!

659
00:33:01.130 --> 00:33:02.880
Ha-ha! Fire up the presses!

660
00:33:02.960 --> 00:33:06.680
The World Economic Journal's got
a scorching hot new front-page story.

661
00:33:06.760 --> 00:33:08.500
And the headline is...

662
00:33:08.580 --> 00:33:13.240
Emperor of the Sea, Straw Hat Luffy Wages
War with the Navy on Egghead and Holds.

663
00:33:13.320 --> 00:33:13.810
War!

664
00:33:13.810 --> 00:33:15.240
And it's Dr.
Vegapunk Hostage!

665
00:33:15.240 --> 00:33:18.000
No better villain than
a pirate, am I right?

666
00:33:18.080 --> 00:33:22.510
Now, when the Government kills Vegapunk,
they won't get any bad publicity!

667
00:33:22.590 --> 00:33:25.240
And they'll be grateful
for my impeccable journalism.

668
00:33:25.310 --> 00:33:27.110
Remind them we
take donations.

669
00:33:27.190 --> 00:33:27.990
[REPORTER A] Yes,
sir! [laughs]

670
00:33:30.240 --> 00:33:31.930
You're not a journalist.

671
00:33:34.440 --> 00:33:36.700
You're just spinning
ridiculous lies!

672
00:33:36.780 --> 00:33:39.060
Luffy would never do
such a horrible thing!

673
00:33:36.790 --> 00:33:38.790
<b>Princess Nefertari Vivi
Kingdom of Alabasta</b>

674
00:33:39.140 --> 00:33:41.320
You and the government
are pathetic!

675
00:33:41.400 --> 00:33:42.090
Vivi!

676
00:33:42.080 --> 00:33:44.000
<b>King Wapol
The Evil Kingdom of Black Drum</b>

677
00:33:42.090 --> 00:33:44.000
Keep your voice down,
are you crazy?

678
00:33:44.080 --> 00:33:46.840
The Government could be listening
to our every word right now!

679
00:33:46.840 --> 00:33:48.870
What if they've got
the whole place bugged?

680
00:33:48.870 --> 00:33:50.810
They're gonna
squash us like bugs!

681
00:33:51.160 --> 00:33:51.930
So zip it!

682
00:33:52.010 --> 00:33:54.210
And don't forget,
Morgy is savin' our asses!

683
00:33:54.250 --> 00:33:55.860
Get off his tailfeathers!

684
00:33:55.940 --> 00:33:56.960
Absolutely not.

685
00:33:57.040 --> 00:33:58.780
I will not be silent about this!

686
00:33:58.860 --> 00:34:01.720
What gives you the right to twist
the truth for your own gain?

687
00:34:01.720 --> 00:34:03.430
Have you no
sense of decency?

688
00:34:03.920 --> 00:34:05.060
[GIRLS squeal]

689
00:34:05.040 --> 00:34:06.950
Those are my clothes
she's wearing, you know!

690
00:34:06.950 --> 00:34:08.660
And I'll never
wash them again!

691
00:34:08.740 --> 00:34:10.460
You're so lucky!

692
00:34:11.020 --> 00:34:13.400
[BOTH] Princess Vivi!

693
00:34:13.910 --> 00:34:16.490
[grunts] You were crying your eyes
out yesterday, little girl!

694
00:34:16.490 --> 00:34:20.110
And today you're all high and mighty
telling me how to do my job?

695
00:34:20.190 --> 00:34:22.010
I'm a mover and a shaker!

696
00:34:22.090 --> 00:34:23.660
A big news maker!

697
00:34:23.740 --> 00:34:24.840
Who are you?

698
00:34:25.340 --> 00:34:27.390
Newspapers are
entertainment!

699
00:34:27.470 --> 00:34:31.140
So I don't care if
they're true or not!

700
00:34:33.980 --> 00:34:34.810
How.
